# Keep build context lean and secrets out of the image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed by the image's own stages — never copy from the host.
vendor

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/auth.json

# Local dev state
/.phpunit.cache
/.phpunit.result.cache
/.idea
/.vscode
/.zed
/.nova
/.cursor
/.codex
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/storage/logs/*
/storage/framework/cache/data/*
/storage/framework/sessions/*
/storage/framework/views/*
/database/*.sqlite

# CI + orchestration files are not needed at runtime.
Jenkinsfile
docker-compose*.yml
deploy/
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
# `*.md` only matches at the root, so nested docs need this or they ship in the
# image via `COPY . .` in the vendor stage.
*.md
/docs
/.opencode
/.claude

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# npm workspaces. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is
# swept into the API image on every build. That is the failure this file exists
# to prevent, and it is silent: the build succeeds, the image just gets bigger.
#
# `**/node_modules`, not a bare `node_modules`. Docker matches a pattern with no
# slash against the root only, so a bare `node_modules` excluded the root install
# and nothing else. npm nests a workspace's own node_modules inside the package
# whenever hoisting conflicts, so `apps/user/node_modules` was reaching the build
# context - and with four Next.js applications that is the bigger half of the
# problem, not the smaller one. The `.gitignore` comment on the same pattern
# already says npm nests; this one has to agree.
**/node_modules

# The generated typed client is NOT excluded, and that is deliberate.
#
# It used to be, on the reasoning recorded here before: "produced fresh by
# `php artisan api-client:generate` in the container, so copying a host copy in
# would defeat the point." That reasoning cannot hold for the API image. It
# installs `--no-dev`, and `laravel/wayfinder` is a `require-dev` dependency, so
# `api-client:generate` is not a command the API image can run at all - nothing
# in the Dockerfile or the entrypoint invokes it. The exclusion therefore
# protected nothing, and it cost something real: the front-end images are built
# from this same context and cannot typecheck or build without these files,
# because @fixmate/api-client re-exports operations that import from them.
#
# The spec's own plan agrees. It has the pipeline generate the client in a
# throwaway PHP container *before* the front-end images are built from the same
# workspace, which only works if the output is in the build context.
#
# What actually keeps the client honest is `php artisan api-client:check`, which
# regenerates into a temp directory and fails on a difference. That runs in CI
# and in the pipeline, where PHP and the dev dependencies are present, and it
# does not depend on this file at all.
#
# The API image now carries a few dozen unused small files. That is the cheaper
# mistake: dead weight in an image nothing reads, versus a front end that cannot
# build.

# Front-end build output. `apps/user` produces the first two of these; the
# other three applications arrive with tickets 15 to 19 and need no change here
# unless they adopt a different bundler. Listed ahead of the applications rather
# than discovered once an image is 200MB larger than it should be.
#
#   **/.next            next dev and next build, per application
#   apps/*/out          next build with output: 'export' (a static export)
#   apps/*/dist         a bundler that emits dist instead of .next
#   **/coverage         test output, from whichever runner a member uses
#   **/.turbo           turbo's cache, if a member adopts it
#
# Every pattern is scoped to `apps/*` or `packages/*` where it can be. A bare
# `out` would mean the ROOT `out/`, which is an rsync test fixture committed to
# prove the Jenkinsfile's --delete staging fix - it is not front-end output, it
# must not be excluded from git, and renaming it is its own commit's business.
# The static export that will collide with it is `apps/user/out`, per
# application, and that is the path above.
**/.next
apps/*/out
apps/*/dist
packages/*/out
packages/*/dist
**/coverage
**/.turbo
